/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Round 10b (baits agent, 2026-11-11): the facts the bait ranking of js/area-gear.js (PsAreaGear.baits) works from.
   Nothing here is a measured catch rate. Each rule says what it rests on:
     basis 'src'  = stated by the page(s) in src (read 2026-11-11, or the app's own catalogue text);
     basis 'rule' = an angler's rule of thumb or our own reasoning from the app's layers: shown in the app with "~" and never as a source.
   traits[id]: points (about -10 … +8) a bait, lure or rig gains or loses.
     light  [dawn, day, dusk, night]          bed { rock, seagrass, coarse, sand, mud } (the seabed class of the cell, data/habitat.js)
     depth  [min, max] m it can be fished in  rough / calm (waves >= 0.8 m / < 0.3 m)   murky / clear   cold / warm (sea < 18.5 / >= 24 °C)
     boat: 1 = from a boat only; shore: 1 = from the shore only; food = what it is or imitates (a diet class below); aid: 1 = not a hook bait;
     lure: 1 / rig: 1 = its kind (else a natural bait); noTemp: 1 = the warm/cold lure rule does not apply (squid jigs, sabiki);
     avail = fish ids whose season (data/species*.js) says when the live or fresh bait is around;
     rl / rn / rc / rr / rw / rb / rd = the rule (below) shown with its light / night / clear-murky-calm / rough / warm-cold / seabed / depth points;
       without one the app shows a plain line ("Good at dusk"), marked as a rule of thumb.
   diet[fish]: 2 = main food, 1 = also eaten, of fish / crust(aceans) / moll(uscs: bivalves, snails) / worm / ceph(alopods) / plant (algae, seagrass,
     detritus). Our reading of the food sentence on the species' FishBase or SeaLifeBase page (the link is built from the scientific name): levels, not
     shares. Read on the page on 2026-11-11: sargos, tsipoura, parrotfish, seabass, melanouri, pandora. The other rows were written from the same
     pages' text as remembered, not re-read: treat them as unverified until someone checks each page. No row for the toadfish (its page states no food)
     or the swordfish (not fished).
   seen: open catch reports that name what the fish took (eval/angler/catches-v2.json; rows printed by scripts/baits/validate.mjs --seen):
     [area id or '', fish, [gear ids], month or 0, source title, url].
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
